- F2 [Major] slot-2 alt mislabels a student-app screen — closed. New D-15a (spec 292-300) marks the alt a draft and keeps PR's wording. The draft mark appears in both entries: the en code comment `// alt draft, see D-15a` (line 572) and the Thai row `... (draft, D-15a)` (line 588). Open question 7 and plan "Answers owed to PR" 4 route it to PR. No contradiction with 6.3 or AC-13.
- F3 [Major] dangling "design rule 3/7/8" citations — closed. All three now resolve in `apps/www-reading-advantage/docs/design-rules.md`: the `shadcn/no-inline-styles` table row (line 13) for D-9, review-checklist item 7 (line 24) for D-11, and item 8 (line 25) for 6.3. No bare "design rule n" citation remains in either file.
- F4 [Nit] conservation in baht floats — closed. AC-3 and plan 1.1 item 4 now pin the check in integer satang: 801,000 + 464,569 = 1,265,569 and 1,201,500 + 669,444 = 1,870,944, with the note that a baht-Number sum fails in float.
- F5 [Nit] overbroad brief-match claim — closed. Spec line 143 now reads "Every money figure in the brief matches this table to the whole baht."
- F6 [Nit] quoted phase number — closed as written. Line 594 now quotes 8/18; the image shows 8/18. The residual label-word mismatch is F7.

## Regression pass

- Money recheck (D-3 algorithm, rate scale 1e9, truncation, exact integer products under 2^53): six check rates reproduce to four decimals (40.5000, 42.5000, 45.0000, 50.0000, 55.6065, 60.6315); asymptote 71.4286%; rate at 1e9 = 71.422028% < 71.43%. Preset 1: 5,520.00 / 165.60 / 5,354.40. Preset 2: rate 52.7321%, gross 12,655.69, legs 8,010.00, payout 4,645.69, tax 139.37, net 4,506.32. Preset 3: rate 56.6953%, gross 18,709.44, legs 12,015.00, payout 6,694.44, tax 200.83, net 6,493.61. All match D-2.
- New satang equalities: the module produces exactly 801,000 + 464,569 = 1,265,569 and 1,201,500 + 669,444 = 1,870,944, so AC-3 and plan 1.1 use figures D-2 produces. The baht float counterexample holds: 8010 + 4645.69 !== 12655.69.
- D-3 reviewed-result line vs D-2: the new guard sentence (172-174) states preset 2 as 12,655.69 / 4,645.69 / 4,506.32 and names the raw-float rounding 12,655.70 / 4,645.70 / 4,506.33 as rejected. No contradiction; the rejected figures appear nowhere as accepted values.
- D-15a and open question 7 vs 6.3 and AC-13: consistent. AC-13's "the copy's alt text" is the pinned draft string; D-15a says the locale test pins it as it stands.
- Plan coherence: task 2.1's Files, Done, and AC-13 agree on the manifest test file; "Answers owed to PR" gained item 4 without disturbing items 1-3; gates, phase tables, and Out of scope are unchanged and consistent.

## Verdict

Nothing blocks Red. Verdict: PASS, with one new Nit (F7) for the author's next edit.

